#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084102} :activity/id #uuid "ec6c85e9-6830-57b2-8009-2f8599700364" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048135 :topic/id #uuid "8257a26c-85bf-580e-9d81-e2194473d981" :topic/math-academy-id 793} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084102 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084442 :tutorial/content "Suppose we roll a fair die. Then, the sample space $\\mathcal S$ of this experiment is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{S} = \\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider the event\n$X = \\{6\\}$.\nThis means that $X$ is the event \"the die lands on $6$.\" We know that\n\n$$\nP(X) = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nbecause there are $6$ equally likely outcomes and only $1$ of those outcomes is a $6$.\n\nWe can represent the entire sample space $\\mathcal S$, the event $X$, and its probability using a **Venn diagram**.\n\n![](images/96/966be6be009751b755fbcaca9f037e0c4ee281525a94e50a9a19631dc7cd4e1f.png)\n\nNote the following important points:\n\n- The area inside the rectangle represents the sample space $\\mathcal S$.\n- The area inside the circle (shaded blue) represents the event $X$.\n- The number inside the blue circle represents the probability of $X$.\n- The area inside the rectangle but outside the circle represents the event $X'$, the complement of $X$. In our case, the complement is\n$X' = \\{1,2,3,4,5\\}$,\nwhich consists of every event other than throwing a $6$.\n\nFor any event $X$, we have\n\n$$\nP(X) +P\\left(X'\\right) = 1\n$$\n\nNote that the above formula can be rearranged into either of the following equivalent forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X) &= 1 - P(X^{′}) \\\\\nP(X^{′}) &= 1 - P(X)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we can calculate\n\n$$\nP\\left(X'\\right)\n$$\n\nas\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X^{′}) &= 1 - P(X) \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the sample space $\\mathcal S$ contains every possible event, we sometimes write\n\n$$\nP(\\mathcal S) = 1\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "af5371a2-dcfe-5de0-b0ab-f82c96a0b759" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3657 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "93f32069-023f-5d69-983e-2273e36c3952" :step/math-academy-id 20492 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084132}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084103 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083212 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083011 :question/id #uuid "c9db939d-eb4f-5516-b95d-666e235a95c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5621"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbb5348e-e292-513f-8b0a-90428692fc0a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049752}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083692} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233268} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234454} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234455}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Probability of the Complement Given the Probability of the Event"} :step/id #uuid "87f1844e-77bf-5d6f-a5cc-5bf66a479b5f" :step/math-academy-id 20495 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084104}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084104 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083213 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083012 :question/id #uuid "fc8c6d6b-1596-5732-afe0-783b176339be" :question/math-academy-id "e-5624"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af4cfa4a-7f49-50c9-a875-ce51c3874c4f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083490} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083491} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234042} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516818} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516821}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Probability of an Event Given the Probability of the Complement"} :step/id #uuid "113d7621-4637-5ddb-bcfe-a8f99fc1bb72" :step/math-academy-id 20502 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084105}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084105 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083214 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083014 :question/id #uuid "a761cb7f-122c-5ca0-8e90-109e0df60f3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5630"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01a9cd80-086d-5667-b4ad-296728e9ec09" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050994}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083694} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083695}] :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Venn Diagram for a Given Sample Space"} :step/id #uuid "ab03ce26-02b2-5bee-a351-687d9a193e8a" :step/math-academy-id 20504} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084132 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083230 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083030 :question/id #uuid "a8f4aa82-b372-5569-804e-ecb8c8ebad4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5722"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "450401ad-3c58-5c15-ab78-b5e1ccf42a85" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049642}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083492} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083693} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233266} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234453}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Venn Diagram is Correct"} :step/id #uuid "c9efaccc-7297-5304-9366-ffdbc569b338" :step/math-academy-id 20705 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084103}}] :activity/title "Venn Diagrams in Probability" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186083470}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516962} :activity/id #uuid "e2fcbe2f-4ff6-58b3-8208-814e82a85124" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048135 :topic/id #uuid "8257a26c-85bf-580e-9d81-e2194473d981" :topic/math-academy-id 793} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516883 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64e91312-ff58-54f3-b439-a8ba0e101cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516332} {:answer/id #uuid "a2568178-6c14-5310-b06c-f6da6cadd369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516446} {:answer/id #uuid "a89f9d8f-ba4e-55a2-9762-c20470143c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516463} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0bbe30-3e25-5367-88f5-88e0431bffb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516541} {:answer/id #uuid "d990847b-1002-5b97-9e33-5b92b5b1594f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516569}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516463} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d3be114-0077-5092-b1f3-6cfed4a013eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516718}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8518694b-ea1e-5380-a35c-13f3072f6df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-84440" :question/problem "![](images/52/5245725446c23cc37e5ca4ad5b4def939c1544100eb3488092f59c4ed0f8beaa.png)\n\nConsider the sample space $S$ with the Venn diagram given above. What is $P(A)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given Venn diagram, we have $P(A)=y$ and $P({A}^{′})=\\frac{y}{22}.$\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A)+P({A}^{′}) & =1 \\\\ y+\\frac{y}{22} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{23y}{22} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{22}{23}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,  $P(A)=y=\\frac{22}{23}.$"} :step/id #uuid "20e5a0d7-e4a4-5527-9522-5eac4387dd43"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516885 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "618e6135-f56b-58e3-9328-1dabdd58e75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.251" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516325} {:answer/id #uuid "98e412be-1a3f-5243-b5d3-e6079198e12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.201" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516428} {:answer/id #uuid "bc95322b-4d62-5251-8e5a-af2d36102789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.551" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516508} {:answer/id #uuid "c03ce4f2-8551-5443-840b-a6936ad84d20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516521} {:answer/id #uuid "d82264de-339c-5e57-9840-e930e1482ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.521" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516325} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee1b406-0379-5d58-ba7e-b9ef815df898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7764a147-f3f7-5293-8ab2-21a4f6d2919a" :question/math-academy-id "q-84435" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a347f23ec8c99fda74de190515eb7aa2d071be29ca106b99116b3d050cb8a1fe.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P(X).$" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P({X}^{′})=0.749.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X) & =1-P({X}^{′}) \\\\  & =1-0.749 \\\\  & =0.251.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2c9093fe-c1c5-5ee0-9d9c-ed832e4df4f4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516883}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516962 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "845355a0-843b-51f7-8c0d-52009b5363fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079812} {:answer/id #uuid "93f57bbd-68cb-5590-b469-f8dec98c1443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079813} {:answer/id #uuid "b495be06-7373-56b0-9303-363912083a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079814} {:answer/id #uuid "f552a0c7-fea4-5002-ae66-4c9943b9551b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079815} {:answer/id #uuid "26fabe08-9668-5bfd-b855-ea3411ba9fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079812} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ccf4c3-ab1b-50f2-bb00-0b00faa94fbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186079811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "991f3941-ac00-506d-94c9-cb69a7d61849" :question/math-academy-id "q-11322" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9c092436e6f2f66cd2ade33818209f001d1481f962c086da09c284975af83795.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P({X}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P(X)=\\frac{2}{5}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{′}) & =1-P(X) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c6e45cc7-205e-57d1-80c2-e67d0fe17e04" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516885}}] :activity/title "Venn Diagrams in Probability" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516110}]}
